' LAS VEGAS HIGH
' The slot machine from Tim Hartnell's Giant Book of Computer Games
' (Ballantine Books, 1984; Interface Publications, 1983), for the
' ColecoVision in Amy by Amy Bienvenu.
'
' You come in with $250. Bet, pull the handle, and the three reels spin.
' Each reel stops on a symbol drawn with the book's odds (out of 43: BAR 2,
' Bell 4, Apple 6, Cherry 8, Lemon 11, Plum 12). The book's payouts, times
' your bet: three BARs 9 ("That's jackpot style!"), three Bells 3.9, three
' of a kind 3.5 (but not three Apples, which the listing pays as a pair),
' a pair 0.7; and on top, a Bell on the right 0.6, an Apple at each end
' 0.5, Cherry-Bell-Cherry 0.4. A win is paid on top of your bet; a loss
' takes the bet. Go broke and the night is over; pass $2,500 and the house
' throws you out ("People with luck like yours give our casino a bad
' name").
'
' Controls (either joystick): left and right change the bet by $10, up
' bets everything; down pulls the handle (or press a side button). On the
' title, up and down choose. Keypad not used.
'
' Liberties taken:
' - The book typed in any bet; here it moves in $10 steps (or all you have
'   when that is less than $10).
' - The listing's favourite combination tests for an Apple in the middle
'   while its message says "cherry, bell, cherry"; here it is the bell, as
'   the message says.
' - The reels, the handle, the lights and the coins are new; the book
'   printed a line of symbol names. New music (Neon Strip) and sounds.
' - The best night (the most money you held) is kept until power off.
'
' House rules kept: text in columns 2-29 and rows 1-22; sprites: the
' handle (two) and up to four coins; the frame loop is protected from the
' NMI and every screen is drawn with the NMI off after a wait.
'
' How the reels turn: see art.py. Each reel window is 4 x 6 tiles of its
' own (codes 184-255, middle third), numbered down each column; a reel at
' place P (0-191) shows lines P to P+47 of the strip, one 48-byte copy per
' column for the patterns and one for the colours.

